/*
 * countries-data.js - starting data for the World 2026 strategy game (game start: January 2026).
 * Keys are ISO 3166-1 numeric codes as 3-digit strings, matching world-atlas@2.0.2 (110m and 50m).
 *
 * Fields: pop = millions (2025); gdp = nominal GDP, bn USD (2025 est.); def = military spending, bn USD;
 * mil = active military personnel, thousands; nukes = estimated warheads; gov = democracy|hybrid|authoritarian;
 * blocs = real memberships as of Jan 2026; approval = game value 0-100 (judgment, not a poll).
 * Extra field on non-sovereign map shapes only: owner = id of the sovereign state.
 *
 * Sources:
 *  - GDP: IMF World Economic Outlook, October 2025 (2025 estimates); missing values (Cuba, Syria, North Korea,
 *    Yemen, Eritrea, territories) are rough estimates.
 *  - Population: UN World Population Prospects 2024 (2025 medium estimate); Israel and Taiwan from national statistics.
 *  - Defense spending: SIPRI Military Expenditure fact sheet, April 2025 (2024 figures, current USD);
 *    countries without SIPRI data (UAE, Qatar, North Korea, etc.) are estimates.
 *  - Active military: IISS The Military Balance 2025 (rounded); some small states estimated.
 *  - Nuclear warheads: SIPRI Yearbook 2025 / FAS Status of World Nuclear Forces 2025 (total inventories).
 *  - Government type: EIU Democracy Index 2024 (full + flawed democracy = democracy).
 *  - Blocs: official membership lists (NATO, EU, CSTO, SCO, BRICS, Arab League, GCC, AU, ASEAN incl. Timor-Leste
 *    from Oct 2025, AUKUS, Quad, CIS). Armenia is still formally in CSTO (participation frozen); suspended AU
 *    members are kept; Moldova left out of CIS (withdrawing); Saudi Arabia not counted in BRICS (never confirmed).
 *  - Military equipment (sovereign states; territories with owner = 0): res = reserve personnel, thousands;
 *    tanks = main battle tanks in active service; afv = other armoured fighting vehicles (IFV/APC/recce, rounded);
 *    art = artillery incl. self-propelled, towed and MLRS, excluding mortars (rounded); air = combat-capable
 *    fighter/attack/bomber aircraft; heli = attack helicopters; ships = principal surface combatants incl. carriers,
 *    destroyers, frigates and corvettes; subs = submarines (all types); carriers = aircraft carriers (Japan's
 *    Izumo/Kaga F-35B conversions and Italy's Cavour, Spain's Juan Carlos I and Thailand's Chakri Naruebet counted;
 *    helicopter-only LHDs not counted); missiles = strategic/ballistic strike level 0-3 (0 none, 1 short-range or
 *    tactical, 2 medium/regional, 3 intercontinental or SLBM); airdef = air-defence quality level 0-3.
 *    Sources: IISS The Military Balance 2025 (main), Global Firepower 2025 and SIPRI as cross-checks; values are
 *    rounded and small forces are estimates. Russia and Ukraine reflect heavy war losses (end-2025 estimates, low
 *    confidence). Syria reflects Israeli strikes on the former regime's arsenal (Dec 2024). Iran's airdef is
 *    lowered to 1 after the 2024-2025 Israeli/US strikes. Levels 0-3 are game judgments, not official ratings.
 *  - Wars: news reports up to Jan 2026. Only Russia-Ukraine is an open interstate war at game start.
 *    Thailand-Cambodia (ceasefire 27 Dec 2025), India-Pakistan (ceasefire May 2025), Israel-Iran (ceasefire June 2025),
 *    Pakistan-Afghanistan (Oct 2025 truce; open war only from 27 Feb 2026) and the 3 Jan 2026 US raid on Venezuela
 *    are reflected as hostile relations instead.
 */

